{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e006498f-033b-4290-bb37-3f3cba321187","hash":"5e62e9041c49d5f981c0504b38d0dc063e05e763c18be983c72320de2379c332","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nCodebase and user instructions are shown below. Be sure to adhere to these instructions. IMPORTANT: These instructions OVERRIDE any default behavior and you MUST follow them exactly as written.\n\nContents of C:\\Users\\pssps\\.claude\\CLAUDE.md (user's private global instructions for all projects):\n\n# oh-my-claudecode - Intelligent Multi-Agent Orchestration\n\nYou are running with oh-my-claudecode (OMC), a multi-agent orchestration layer for Claude Code.\nCoordinate specialized agents, tools, and skills so work is completed accurately and efficiently.\n\n<operating_principles>\n- Delegate specialized work to the most appropriate agent.\n- Prefer evidence over assumptions: verify outcomes before final claims.\n- Choose the lightest-weight path that preserves quality.\n- Consult official docs before implementing with SDKs/frameworks/APIs.\n</operating_principles>\n\n<delegation_rules>\nDelegate for: multi-file changes, refactors, debugging, reviews, planning, research, verification.\nWork directly for: trivial ops, small clarifications, single commands.\nRoute code to `executor` (use `model=opus` for complex work). Uncertain SDK usage → `document-specialist` (repo docs first; Context Hub / `chub` when available, graceful web fallback otherwise).\n</delegation_rules>\n\n<model_routing>\n`haiku` (quick lookups), `sonnet` (standard), `opus` (architecture, deep analysis).\nDirect writes OK for: `~/.claude/**`, `.omc/**`, `.claude/**`, `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`.\n</model_routing>\n\n<skills>\nInvoke via `/oh-my-claudecode:<name>`. Trigger patterns auto-detect keywords.\nTier-0 workflows include `autopilot`, `ultrawork`, `ralph`, `team`, and `ralplan`.\nKeyword triggers: `\"autopilot\"→autopilot`, `\"ralph\"→ralph`, `\"ulw\"→ultrawork`, `\"ccg\"→ccg`, `\"ralplan\"→ralplan`, `\"deep interview\"→deep-interview`, `\"deslop\"`/`\"anti-slop\"`→ai-slop-cleaner, `\"deep-analyze\"`→analysis mode, `\"tdd\"`→TDD mode, `\"deepsearch\"`→codebase search, `\"ultrathink\"`→deep reasoning, `\"cancelomc\"`→cancel.\nTeam orchestration is explicit via `/team`.\nDetailed agent catalog, tools, team pipeline, commit protocol, and full skills registry live in the native `omc-reference` skill when skills are available, including reference for `explore`, `planner`, `architect`, `executor`, `designer`, and `writer`; this file remains sufficient without skill support.\n</skills>\n\n<verification>\nVerify before claiming completion. Size appropriately: small→haiku, standard→sonnet, large/security→opus.\nIf verification fails, keep iterating.\n</verification>\n\n<execution_protocols>\nBroad requests: explore first, then plan. 2+ independent tasks in parallel. `run_in_background` for builds/tests.\nKeep authoring and review as separate passes: writer pass creates or revises content, reviewer/verifier pass evaluates it later in a separate lane.\nNever self-approve in the same active context; use `code-reviewer` or `verifier` for the approval pass.\nBefore concluding: zero pending tasks, tests passing, verifier evidence collected.\n</execution_protocols>\n\n<hooks_and_context>\nHooks inject `<system-reminder>` tags. Key patterns: `hook success: Success` (proceed), `[MAGIC KEYWORD: ...]` (invoke skill), `The boulder never stops` (ralph/ultrawork active).\nPersistence: `<remember>` (7 days), `<remember priority>` (permanent).\nKill switches: `DISABLE_OMC`, `OMC_SKIP_HOOKS` (comma-separated).\n</hooks_and_context>\n\n<cancellation>\n`/oh-my-claudecode:cancel` ends execution modes. Cancel when done+verified or blocked. Don't cancel if work incomplete.\n</cancellation>\n\n<worktree_paths>\nState: `.omc/state/`, `.omc/state/sessions/{sessionId}/`, `.omc/notepad.md`, `.omc/project-memory.json`, `.omc/plans/`, `.omc/research/`, `.omc/logs/`\n</worktree_paths>\n\n## Setup\n\nSay \"setup omc\" or run `/oh-my-claudecode:omc-setup`.\n\nContents of C:\\Users\\pssps\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-pssps-Documents-Projects-sc4sap-project\\memory\\MEMORY.md (user's auto-memory, persists across conversations):\n\n- [Feedback: MD 200-line limit](feedback_md_line_limit.md) — Skill/agent/rule MD files ≤ 200 lines HARD. At 201 lines always split to companion file. If post-split any file still > 200, WARN user explicitly. Exempt: README, CLAUDE.md, plain docs\n- [Feedback: Skill MD files — English-first](feedback_skill_md_language.md) — skills/*/*.md must be English; no Korean in prompts, examples, or templates (international audience)\n- [User: owns 3-layer SAP MCP stack](user_role_plugin_developer.md) — sc4sap plugin + abap-mcp-adt-powerup MCP server + @babamba2/mcp-abap-adt-clients library all under user's control; fix at the correct semantic layer\n- [Feedback: verify issue hypotheses before coding](feedback_verify_issue_hypotheses.md) — multi-cause issue reports are hypotheses, not facts; read the accused code path + run one diagnostic query + confirm scope with user before implementing any of them\n- [Feedback: verify locally before publish/push](feedback_verify_before_publish.md) — before npm publish / git push to main / marketplace release: npm pack + install + smoke test in real target first; user explicitly prefers verify-first default\n- [Feedback: Ask before npm (network blocked)](feedback_npm_network_gate.md) — npm network cuts off HKT; prove npm is actually needed (offline dep check) before asking user to switch\n- [Feedback: No company initials in public docs](feedback_no_company_initials_in_docs.md) — never use initials that could read as real companies (HK=Hankook, SS=Samsung, LG, etc.) in public docs/examples; use ISO country codes (KR, US, DE)\n- [Feedback: No customer specifics in CHANGELOG](feedback_no_customer_specifics_in_changelog.md) — public CHANGELOG/README must not list customer system names (HKT-DEV) + customer Z* impl names (ZSD_*, ZMM_*) together; validation specifics belong in commit body / project memory only\n- [Reference: sc4sap 3-location sync](reference_sc4sap_source_locations.md) — patch project source (`~/Documents/Projects/sc4sap_project/sc4sap/`) + marketplace + cache together; cache folder that runs = `installPath` in installed_plugins.json (0.6.35 since 2026-10-14, was misnamed 0.6.14)\n- [Project: DDIC ECC MCP integration status](project_ddic_ecc_integration_status.md) — validated 2026-04-22 on HKT-DEV: CreateDomain/CreateDataElement → path=ecc-odata-rfc, status=active; Domain+DataElement(domain) full, Table Create/Update inform-only\n- [Feedback: Vendor patch — diff version first](feedback_vendor_patch_version_check.md) — before copying vendor/ contents, diff package.json version; dist-only copy OK if match, else full vendor replace (node_modules included)\n- [Feedback: project/sc4sap/vendor edit forbidden](feedback_project_vendor_noedit.md) — sc4sap project vendor/abap-mcp-adt is bridge-bootstrap dev clone, not SoT; edit at marketplaces/abap-mcp-adt-powerup, mirror outward\n- [Project: v0.6.7 enforcement reverted in 0.6.8](project_v067_enforcement_broken.md) — reverted 2026-04-24 via `a5fbfcf`; frontmatter `model:` now declarative-only. Constraint: Agent tool is main-thread-only — any redesign must work within that.\n- [Reference: Claude Code subagent tool scoping](reference_subagent_architecture.md) — Agent/Task tool is main-thread-only; general-purpose sub-agents lack SAP MCP; name= addressability is ephemeral (use UUID for cross-turn)\n- [Project: Keychain distribution RESOLVED (0.6.9 + 0.6.11)](project_keychain_migration_pending.md) — bundled runtime-deps/keyring/ (5cd97ea) + offline integrity verify (607d4bc) + CI gate; archival reference to historical gap\n- [Project: active branch is now shared (2+ committers)](project_active_branch_shared.md) — since 2026-04-24: NO force-push / NO amend-push on active; plain push only; rebase limited to unpushed commits.\n- [Reference: /plugin reads .claude-plugin version fields](reference_claude_plugin_version_source.md) — Claude Code marketplace surfaces version from plugin.json + marketplace.json (3 fields total), NOT package.json; bump all three at every release (CI now cross-checks against package.json)\n- [Reference: MD line endings vary (autocrlf)](reference_skill_md_crlf.md) — LF in git, CRLF on disk/synced copies; frontmatter regex must use \\r?\\n; compare copies with CR stripped\n- [Project: pending commits 2026-09-17](project_pending_commits_2026_09_17.md) — sc4sap 0.6.22 + abap-mcp-adt-powerup 4.8.7 released 2026-09-22; only sc4sap_web still uncommitted; plan in sc4sap_project/PENDING_COMMITS.md\n- [Project: teamMode rollout status + pending runtime validations](project_teammode_rollout_status.md) — Phase 4 Type A fully validated (3 live tests); Phase 5-7 docs committed c2822db + pending Phase 6/7 commit; runtime validation blocked on SAP auth. Target object: ZSDR03000 for Phase 5.\n- [Reference: MCP vendor launcher freezes SAP_PASSWORD at boot](reference_mcp_stale_password_env.md) — activateProfile() is one-shot at startup; sap.env/keychain edits need full Claude Code restart (not just /mcp reconnect). Explains recurring 401 after account unlock. ReloadProfile does NOT rebind the ADT client (BaseMcpServer cache) nor clear SAP_RFC_ODATA_* — restart after every profile switch (2026-10-14).\n- [Feedback: teammate shutdown_request reliability](feedback_teammate_shutdown_bug.md) — SendMessage shutdown only works if teammate was actively running; idle teammates ignore it even with <Team_Shutdown_Handler>. Best effort, expect leftover members. Fresh session = clean slate.\n- [Feedback: sc4sap skill subagent_type prefix](feedback_sc4sap_subagent_prefix.md) — every Agent() dispatch in sc4sap skill MDs MUST use `\"sc4sap:sap-<name>\"` — bare `\"sap-<name>\"` fails at runtime due to Claude Code plugin auto-namespacing\n- [Project: critical-review mode prototype (deferred)](project_critical_review_mode.md) — after Phase 5-7 validation: opt-in 3-reviewer consensus mode for analyze-code (`critical` arg). executor stays split-only. Decision data needed from Phase 5-7 token metrics first.\n- [Feedback: Entire-Checkpoint trailer in every commit](feedback_entire_checkpoint_trailer.md) — `entire attach` only registers metadata; commit trailer must be added manually. Fetch via `entire sessions list`. Forgetting it (incident 2026-04-26 commit 1f4c5bf) drops the commit out of entire tracking, and post-hoc fix is blocked by no-force-push policy on shared branches.\n- [Project: MCP self-heal Pass 1b](project_mcp_selfheal_pass1b.md) — `npm install --omit=dev` can silently skip root deps from a stale lockfile (pino observed on 0.6.11→0.6.14); bridge/mcp-server.cjs has explicit-name fallback added 2026-04-29\n- [Feedback: Destructive test ops need per-call approval](feedback_destructive_test_preapproval.md) — Delete/Drop/Truncate against SAP requires explicit per-execution approval; never delete SAP-standard objects, copy to Z* alias first\n- [Feedback: User visual verification before close](feedback_user_visual_verify_before_close.md) — SAP-side mutation tasks: mechanical/XML-state OK ≠ done. Set in_progress with \"Awaiting user verification of <X> in <tcode>\" + explicit expected outcome, wait for user confirm before marking completed\n- [Feedback: SmartForms — patch only UI-visible attrs](reference_smartforms_hidden_attrs.md) — HARD RULE: never patch XML attrs that aren't exposed in SE71/SMARTFORMS Form Painter UI (e.g., NUMB_MODE/NUMB_TYPE). User must always be able to see/audit/undo via standard SAP tools. Invisible patches break trust + maintainability\n- [Reference: SSF_CHECK doesn't catch Form Painter break](reference_smartforms_check_limits.md) — SSF_CHECK pass ≠ form openable in SE71. WTYPE T→F on existing window passes SSF_CHECK but breaks Form Painter (RC=1 SFP_DESIGN_START NR=1a). Confirmed Apr 2026 on YSD_PACK_LIST WT001. Final verification must include Form Painter open by user\n- [Reference: SmartForms STYLE_NAME validity](reference_smartforms_style_name_validity.md) — STYLE_NAME must reference a real SmartStyle in STXSADM/STXFADM; non-existent value (\"SYSTEM\") leaves XML byte-correct but SE71 silently shows blank. Same risk applies to STDSTYLE, field refs, ADDRNR, graphic NAME. Validate against system before patching.\n- [Project: SmartForms campaign — ABANDONED 2026-05-24](project_smartforms_test_status.md) — full discontinuation. Local rolled back to superclaude-for-sap/active + abap-mcp-adt-powerup/main (rfcBackend lazy fix kept). reference_smartforms_*.md stays as lessons.\n- [Reference: SmartForms activation semantics](reference_smartforms_activation.md) — Activation = STORE(im_active='X'). PATCH/UPLOAD는 inactive 저장만. Unknown format = silent skip + warning (activation 통과 ≠ 적용). SE71 final gate.\n- [Reference: SmartForms MCP dispatcher actions](reference_smartforms_dispatcher_actions.md) — ZMCP_ADT_DISPATCH 액션 catalog (SSF_* + 정확한 param names). /ui2/cl_json silently ignores unknown fields → param 이름 틀리면 false-alarm `TR_TADIR sy-subrc=1` (SU01 락 아님).\n- [Reference: SmartForms format lookup + SmartStyle](reference_smartforms_format_lookup.md) — character/paragraph format은 form-level STDSTYLE에서 lookup. SSF_READ_STYLE active flag = 'A' (not 'X' — silent 0/0). YSD_PACK_LIST: 7 para + 2 char (A2=Bold).\n- [Project: S4-DEV YSD_PACK_LIST — superseded](project_s4dev_smartform_import_inflight.md) — superseded by full SmartForms abandonment 2026-05-24. SAP-side leftover installs (dispatcher 19 actions + ZMCP_SSF FUGR + ZSMCP_BLOB_STAGE on S4-DEV; SSF_* on HKT-DEV) remain present but unused.\n- [Reference: abap-mcp-adt-powerup runtime path](reference_abap_mcp_powerup_runtime_path.md) — bridge loads `cache/sc4sap/.../vendor/abap-mcp-adt/dist/`, NOT `marketplaces/abap-mcp-adt-powerup/dist/`. After build:fast, must mirror dist/** to cache vendor before restart (else MCP runs OLD code).\n- [Project: sc4sap_web = tennto/SC4SAP-PoC clone](project_sc4sap_web_poc_repo.md) — Agent SDK + Next.js PoC, shared with another dev; babamba2 can push since 2026-09 (re-check perms first); plugin_module updated via upstream diff, not copy; web profile = HKT-DEV since 2026-09-29\n- [Reference: workstation latency baseline](reference_workstation_latency_baseline.md) — PC slowness = filter-driver latency, not resources: process launch 126ms (5-12×), user-file open 12.6ms (40-250×) vs System32 1.3ms. Arena Messenger + SearchIndexer ruled out by measurement\n- [Reference: Agent SDK canUseTool is not a chokepoint](reference_agent_sdk_canusetool_gap.md) — built-in tools (Bash/Write/WebFetch) bypass canUseTool entirely even with allowedTools empty; only a PreToolUse hook gates every call. Deny by default, don't list dangerous names\n- [Project: sc4sap_web backend fragilities + highlighting](project_sc4sap_web_session_2026_09_11.md) — discoverToolPolicy runs once at boot with NO retry (prompt storm if MCP is slow); Shiki JS engine is byte-identical to WASM so no oniguruma; grammars need `npm run grammars:refresh`\n- [Feedback: bridge probe triggers npm](feedback_bridge_probe_triggers_npm.md) — launching bridge/mcp-server.cjs (not --check) auto-runs npm self-heal; use --check + MCP log instead, ask before full launch\n- [Reference: Bash heredoc eats backslashes](reference_bash_heredoc_backslash.md) — doubled backslashes in a quoted heredoc collapse to one here (a regex got a backspace char); write backslash code with the Write tool; python3 is a hanging Store stub\n- [Project: 0.6.23 release follow-ups](project_release_0623_followups.md) — cache 0.6.23 not staged (ask npm vs copy), settings.local.json gate entries removed 2026-09-28, DEV test obj ZDE_SC4SAP_TT01, remaining agent tool trims\n- [Reference: skill vs agent model override](reference_skill_model_override.md) — SKILL.md `model:` registered but NOT applied on CLI 2.1.283 (verify via transcript \"model\"); agent aliases applied; effort omitted = per-model default not session; agent defs need restart\n- [Project: 2026-09-28 changes committed 7e9e313](project_pending_restart_validation_2026_09_28.md) — dispatch-mode/aliases/effort/teamMode/HUD pricing committed on active, NOT pushed; synced 3 locations; probe passed\n- [Project: 0.6.25 all skills model: inherit](project_release_0625_inherit.md) — 270ec49+9d1eba3 pushed to origin/active with 0.6.26; SDK checks passed; sc4sap_web branch feat/plugin-0.6.25 (0195fde+80cbebf) not pushed\n- [Project: 0.6.27 Claude Code 2.1.285 spec alignment](project_release_0627_spec_alignment.md) — released active+main 2026-09-30; open: FEATURES \"SAP-Specific Hooks\" section lists nonexistent hooks; stray C:\\c\\ folder\n- [Project: 0.6.28–0.6.29 button flows + screens released](project_release_0628_button_flows.md) — 0.6.29 main cb27f52, 3 locations synced; open: GetMessageClass MCP tool for ECC, west-vertex label ambiguity, keep `_md/`\n- [Project: 0.6.26 selection mockup schema](project_release_0626_selection_schema.md) — on origin/active 79793cd + main 08a1db5, marketplace clone clean at main; open: xlsx selection/ALV overlap; dock declined\n- [Project: 0.6.30 program-to-manual + Signature released](project_program_to_manual_commit.md) — main a6b81ea CI green, 3 locations synced; sc4sap_web 6484f09 committed not pushed, plugin_module lacks 0.6.29/0.6.30\n- [Feedback: reply in Korean](feedback_reply_in_korean.md) — user writes Korean → whole reply in Korean (tables, summaries, status lines); only paths/code/SAP identifiers stay as-is\n- [Project: manual edit mode (Quill) — 0.6.31](project_manual_edit_mode.md) — released 0.6.31 (main 9909e13): excel screen kind + English companion + in-page editor; test IndexedDB via CDP not virtual-time\n- [Reference: sc4sap_web launch shell](reference_sc4sap_web_launch_shell.md) — start backend from Bash; PowerShell `*>` launch breaks tool discovery (0 read tools, ProcessTransport not ready)\n- [Project: 0.6.33–0.6.34 flow editor + field figures released](project_flow_editor_pending_sync.md) — main 49a5753 CI green, 3 locations synced; open: Desktop ko-edited.html not imported, web plugin_module behind\n- [Project: 0.6.32 trust-session Read/Edit rules](project_release_0632_trust_session_rules.md) — main aa5a1ad CI green, 3 locations synced; web origin/main 0.5.8 (883ed9e) carries plugin_module 0.6.35 as of 2026-10-14 (local main ff.d); web install-statusline.mjs has fileURLToPath fix not upstreamed\n- [Project: RunUnitTest legacy fix committed](project_runUnitTest_legacy_fix_inflight.md) — superseded: lib 3.15.0 + server 4.8.11 published 2026-10-12 (ECC where-used/activation/GUI status fixes)\n- [Reference: RunUnitTest legacy gaps — RESOLVED](reference_runUnitTest_legacy_gaps.md) — fixed; verified 2026-10-12 on HKT-DEV (PROG container, synchronous run_result inline)\n- [Project: ZSDR24730 design intent](project_zsdr24730_design_intent.md) — repeat SO conversion of same group is intended; OPEQT check is the guard\n- [Project: 0.6.35 customizations + MCP 4.8.9 released](project_customizations_ecc_handoff.md) — ECC table reads, GGB/BTE fixed, VOFM; GGB = creator≠SAP, VOFM = customer range only; web plugin_module ported (web 0.5.8)\n- [Project: Opus 5.5 routing — released in 0.6.36](project_opus55_routing_restart_test.md) — shipped with 0.6.36 (main b76f624, 2026-10-15); open ECC GetEnhancements 404 / GetView DB-view miss\n- [Reference: GetWhereUsed 404 on ECC = lib bug](reference_ecc_whereused_404.md) — 7.40 has usageReferences search but no /scope sub-endpoint; DDIC needs VIT URIs; parser prefix bug; fix in client lib 3.15.0\n- [Project: CBO reference graph design](project_reference_graph_design.md) — 2026-10-12 approved: script edge extraction, std SAP objects as leaf nodes, graph.json next to inventory, P1→P4; package-to-process core = business flow\n- [Feedback: no globs into positional CLIs](feedback_no_glob_into_positional_cli.md) — 2026-10-12 a glob made md-to-html overwrite a user spec .md (recovered byte-identical); name exact files, test output to scratchpad, back up .sc4sap targets first\n- [Project: tcode usage (ST03N) feature](project_tcode_usage_feature.md) — ZMCP_WL FM + WlTcodeUsage OData + MCP GetTcodeUsage on HKT-DEV/YCOMM4/HKDK9A2OE2; DEV keeps only 3 months; GetTcodeUsage + GetJobUsage passed 2026-10-12 (DEV job history only since 09-28); next: used-object list\n- [Project: BASIS 7.31 helpers on ES-DEV](project_basis731_helpers.md) — BXD TR BXDK940378 / pkg ZCOMM2; no Gateway/ui2-json/infosystem → soap + ZCL_MCP_JSON; sticky stateful session fix; install in progress\n- [Project: config-to-document released 0.6.36 + 0.6.37](project_config_to_document.md) — 0.6.37 main 5f2e897 (2026-10-15): edit mode covers view tables, history, screenshots; MM notes done; 7.31 dispatcher pending; main push bypasses PR rule\n- [Project: interface mapping spec — released 0.6.38](project_interface_mapping_spec.md) — main e20cc1e CI green, 3 locations synced; new-interface first, ▸ group rows per carrier, src/tgt colours; test FMs ZSD008 ZSD_RFC*\n</system-reminder>"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# userEmail\nThe user's email address is psspss1122@gmail.com. Use it only to identify the user, such as for authorship, attribution, or filtering their own work. Never send it to an unrelated service, such as in a request header, URL, or payload, unless the user explicitly asks.\n\nClaude Code attached this context automatically; it isn't part of the user's message. It describes the user's own account and workspace, so they don't need it reported back.\n</system-reminder>"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nAttribution for git commits and pull requests you create from here on (this replaces Claude Code's own earlier attribution guidance, such as a previous copy of this reminder; the user's own instructions about these lines, such as a CLAUDE.md or memory rule, take precedence over this reminder, but do not add attribution lines this reminder leaves out):\n- End git commit messages with:\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LpUJqpaXx2sJuYfquskfwF\n- End pull request descriptions with:\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01LpUJqpaXx2sJuYfquskfwF\n\nThe user can follow this conversation from another device; to put a file in front of them there (a report, a screenshot, a built artifact), send it with SendUserFile.\n</system-reminder>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"TR은 내가 출근해야 만들수 있을거라 커밋 푸시, PP작업 부터 하자"}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"e006498f-033b-4290-bb37-3f3cba321187","hash":"3e388097b2ca1c0c4bf87266ab5feafe7a1ad5139642f2d54c86a2aee928aab4","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note: C:\\Users\\pssps\\Documents\\Projects\\sc4sap_project\\sc4sap\\scripts\\config\\extract-config.mjs was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n\nNote: C:\\Users\\pssps\\Documents\\Projects\\sc4sap_project\\sc4sap\\scripts\\extract-customizations.mjs was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\pssps\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\C--Users-pssps-Documents-Projects-sc4sap-project\\\\e006498f-033b-4290-bb37-3f3cba321187\\\\scratchpad\\\\badi-probe.mjs\"}\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// Probe BAdI implementation reads on ECC: the MCP tool and the repository tables through TABLE_READ.\n2\timport { pathToFileURL } from 'url';\n3\tconst { connect, readTable } = await import(pathToFileURL('C:/Users/pssps/.claude/plugins/cache/sc4sap/sc4sap/0.6.35/scripts/config/sap-reader.mjs').href);\n4\tconst c = await connect('badi-probe');\n5\tconst call = async (name, args) => { const r = await c.callTool({ name, arguments: args }); return { err: !!r.isError, text: (r.content?.[0]?.text || '').slice(0, 400) }; };\n6\tconsole.log('GetBadiImplementations', JSON.stringify(await call('GetBadiImplementations', { badi_definition: 'BADI_SD_SALES', customer_only: true, active_only: true, include_methods: false })));\n7\tconsole.log('GetEnhancementSpot', JSON.stringify(await call('GetEnhancementSpot', { enhancement_spot_name: 'BADI_SD_SALES' })));\n8\tfor (const [t, w] of [['SXC_EXIT', { IMP_NAME: { like: 'Z%' } }], ['SXC_ATTR', { IMP_NAME: { like: 'Z%' } }], ['SXC_CLASS', { IMP_NAME: { like: 'Z%' } }], ['SXS_ATTR', { EXIT_NAME: 'BADI_SD_SALES' }], ['ENHHEADER', { ENHNAME: { like: 'Z%' } }], ['BADIIMPL_ENH', { ENHNAME: { like: 'Z%' } }], ['ENHOBJ', { ENHNAME: { like: 'Z%' } }]]) {\n9\t  const r = await readTable(c, t, { where: w, maxRows: 5 });\n10\t  console.log(t, r.ok ? `ok rows=${r.rows.length} trunc=${r.truncated} ${JSON.stringify(r.rows[0] || {}).slice(0, 300)}` : `ERR ${String(r.error).slice(0, 200)}`);\n11\t}\n12\tawait c.close();\n13\t\n\nNote: C:\\Users\\pssps\\Documents\\Projects\\sc4sap_project\\sc4sap\\CHANGELOG.md was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n\nNote: C:\\Users\\pssps\\Documents\\Projects\\sc4sap_project\\sc4sap\\skills\\config-to-document\\SKILL.md was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n\nThe following skills were invoked EARLIER in this session (before the conversation was compacted), not on the current turn. They are shown here for context only so you remain aware of their guidelines.\n\nIMPORTANT: Do NOT re-execute these skills or perform their one-time setup actions (e.g., scheduling, creating files) again. Any request or argument text embedded in the skill bodies below — for example under a \"## User Request\" or \"## Input\" heading — was captured when that skill was first invoked. It is NOT the user's current message and NOT a new request: do not act on it as if it were live. Only continue to apply ongoing behavioral guidelines from these skills where still relevant.\n\n### Skill: update-config\nPath: bundled:update-config\n\n# Update Config Skill\n\nModify Claude Code configuration by updating settings.json files.\n\n## When Hooks Are Required (Not Memory)\n\nIf the user wants something to happen automatically in response to an EVENT, they need a **hook** configured in settings.json. Memory/preferences cannot trigger automated actions.\n\n**These require hooks:**\n- \"Before compacting, ask me what to preserve\" → PreCompact hook\n- \"After writing files, run prettier\" → PostToolUse hook with Write|Edit matcher\n- \"When I run bash commands, log them\" → PreToolUse hook with Bash matcher\n- \"Always run tests after code changes\" → PostToolUse hook\n\n**Hook events:** PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PreCompact, PostCompact, Stop, Notification, SessionStart\n\n## CRITICAL: Read Before Write\n\n**Always read the existing settings file before making changes.** Merge new settings with existing ones - never replace the entire file.\n\n## CRITICAL: Use AskUserQuestion for Ambiguity\n\nWhen the user's request is ambiguous, use AskUserQuestion to clarify:\n- Which settings file to modify (user/project/local)\n- Whether to add to existing arrays or replace them\n- Specific values when multiple options exist\n\n## Decision: /config command vs Direct Edit\n\n**Suggest the `/config` slash command** for these simple settings:\n- `theme`, `editorMode`, `verbose`, `model`\n- `language`, `alwaysThinkingEnabled`\n- `permissions.defaultMode`\n\n**Edit settings.json directly** for:\n- Hooks (PreToolUse, PostToolUse, etc.)\n- Complex permission rules (allow/deny arrays)\n- Environment variables\n- MCP server configuration\n- Plugin configuration\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Clarify intent** - Ask if the request is ambiguous\n2. **Read existing file** - Use Read tool on the target settings file\n3. **Merge carefully** - Preserve existing settings, especially arrays\n4. **Edit file** - Use Edit tool (if file doesn't exist, ask user to create it first)\n5. **Confirm** - Tell user what was changed\n\n## Merging Arrays (Important!)\n\nWhen adding to permission arrays or hook arrays, **merge with existing**, don't replace:\n\n**WRONG** (replaces existing permissions):\n```json\n{ \"permissions\": { \"allow\": [\"Bash(npm *)\"] } }\n```\n\n**RIGHT** (preserves existing + adds new):\n```json\n{\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"allow\": [\n      \"Bash(git *)\",      // existing\n      \"Edit(.claude)\",    // existing\n      \"Bash(npm *)\"       // new\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Settings File Locations\n\nChoose the appropriate file based on scope:\n\n| File | Scope | Git | Use For |\n|------|-------|-----|---------|\n| `~/.claude/settings.json` | Global | N/A | Personal preferences for all projects |\n| `.claude/settings.json` | Project | Commit | Team-wide hooks, permissions, plugins |\n| `.claude/settings.local.json` | Project | Gitignore | Personal overrides for this project |\n\nSettings load in order: user → project → local (later overrides earlier).\n\n## Settings Schema Reference\n\n### Permissions\n```json\n{\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"allow\": [\"Bash(npm *)\", \"Edit(.claude)\", \"Read\"],\n    \"deny\": [\"Bash(rm -rf *)\"],\n    \"ask\": [\"Edit(//etc/*)\"],\n    \"defaultMode\": \"default\" | \"plan\" | \"acceptEdits\" | \"dontAsk\",\n    \"additionalDirectories\": [\"/extra/dir\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Permission Rule Syntax:**\n- Exact match: `\"Bash(npm run test)\"`\n- Prefix wildcard: `\"Bash(git *)\"` - matches `git`, `git status`, `git commit`, etc.\n- Tool only: `\"Read\"` - allows all Read operations\n- File paths: `\"Edit(src/**)\"` - path rules in `permissions` use `Edit(path)` for every file-writing tool (Write, Edit, NotebookEdit) and `Read(path)` for reads. `Write(path)`, `NotebookEdit(path)` and `Glob(path)` rules are not matched by file permission checks. Bare tool names (`\"Write\"`), deny/ask `Tool(param:value)` rules and hook `if` conditions still use each tool's own name\n\n### Environment Variables\n```json\n{\n  \"env\": {\n    \"DEBUG\": \"true\",\n    \"MY_API_KEY\": \"value\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Model & Agent\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": \"sonnet\",  // or \"fable\", \"opus\", \"haiku\", full model ID\n  \"agent\": \"agent-name\",\n  \"alwaysThinkingEnabled\": true\n}\n```\n\n### Attribution (Commits & PRs)\n```json\n{\n  \"attribution\": {\n    \"commit\": \"Custom commit trailer text\",\n    \"pr\": \"Custom PR description text\"\n  }\n}\n```\nSet `commit` or `pr` to empty string `\"\"` to hide that attribution. To hide all of it, set both to `\"\"` and also set `\"sessionUrl\": false`. Write this object form, not `\"attribution\": false`: older Claude Code versions reject true or false here and then skip the whole settings file.\n\n### MCP Server Management\n```json\n{\n  \"enableAllProjectMcpServers\": true,\n  \"enabledMcpjsonServers\": [\"server1\", \"server2\"],\n  \"disabledMcpjsonServers\": [\"blocked-server\"]\n}\n```\n\n### Plugins\n```json\n{\n  \"enabledPlugins\": {\n    \"formatter@anthropic-tools\": true\n  }\n}\n```\nPlugin syntax: `plugin-name@source` where source is `claude-code-marketplace`, `claude-plugins-official`, or `builtin`.\n\n### Other Settings\n- `language`: Preferred response language (e.g., \"japanese\")\n- `cleanupPeriodDays`: Days to keep transcripts before automatic cleanup (default: 30; minimum 1)\n- `respectGitignore`: Whether to respect .gitignore (default: true)\n- `spinnerTipsEnabled`: Show tips in spinner\n- `timeFormat`: Clock format for times shown in the UI: \"auto\" (default), \"12-hour\", \"24-hour\", \"24-hour-utc\", or a strftime pattern such as \"%H:%M\"\n- `timeZone`: IANA time zone for times shown in the UI, e.g. \"UTC\" (default: system time zone)\n- `spinnerVerbs`: Customize spinner verbs (`{ \"mode\": \"append\" | \"replace\", \"verbs\": [...] }`)\n- `spinnerTipsOverride`: Override spinner tips (`{ \"excludeDefault\": true, \"tips\": [\"Custom tip\"] }`)\n- `syntaxHighlightingDisabled`: Disable diff highlighting\n\n\n## Hooks Configuration\n\nHooks run commands at specific points in Claude Code's lifecycle.\n\n### Hook Structure\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"EVENT_NAME\": [\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"ToolName|OtherTool\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"your-command-here\",\n            \"timeout\": 60,\n            \"statusMessage\": \"Running...\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Hook Events\n\n| Event | Matcher | Purpose |\n|-------|---------|---------|\n| PermissionRequest | Tool name | Run before permission prompt |\n| PreToolUse | Tool name | Run before tool, can block |\n| PostToolUse | Tool name | Run after successful tool |\n| PostToolUseFailure | Tool name | Run after tool fails |\n| Notification | Notification type | Run on notifications |\n| Stop | - | Run when Claude stops (including clear, resume, compact) |\n| PreCompact | \"manual\"/\"auto\" | Before compaction |\n| PostCompact | \"manual\"/\"auto\" | After compaction (receives summary) |\n| UserPromptSubmit | - | When user submits |\n| SessionStart | - | When session starts |\n\n**Common tool matchers:** `Bash`, `Write`, `Edit`, `Read`, `Glob`, `Grep`\n\n### Hook Types\n\n**1. Command Hook** - Runs a shell command:\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"prettier --write $FILE\", \"timeout\": 30 }\n```\n\n**2. Prompt Hook** - Evaluates a condition with LLM:\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"prompt\", \"prompt\": \"Is this safe? $ARGUMENTS\" }\n```\nOnly available for tool events: PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PermissionRequest.\n\n**3. Agent Hook** - Runs an agent with tools:\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"agent\", \"prompt\": \"Verify tests pass: $ARGUMENTS\" }\n```\nOnly available for tool events: PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PermissionRequest.\n\n### Hook Input (stdin JSON)\n```json\n{\n  \"session_id\": \"abc123\",\n  \"tool_name\": \"Write\",\n  \"tool_input\": { \"file_path\": \"/path/to/file.txt\", \"content\": \"...\" },\n  \"tool_response\": { \"success\": true }  // PostToolUse only\n}\n```\n\n### Hook JSON Output\n\nHooks can return JSON to control behavior:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"systemMessage\": \"Warning shown to user in UI\",\n  \"continue\": false,\n  \"stopReason\": \"Message shown when blocking\",\n  \"suppressOutput\": false,\n  \"decision\": \"block\",\n  \"reason\": \"Explanation for decision\",\n  \"hookSpecificOutput\": {\n    \"hookEventName\": \"PostToolUse\",\n    \"additionalContext\": \"Context injected back to model\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Fields:**\n- `systemMessage` - Display a message to the user (all hooks)\n- `continue` - Set to `false` to block/stop (default: true)\n- `stopReason` - Message shown when `continue` is false\n- `suppressOutput` - Hide stdout from transcript (default: false)\n- `decision` - \"block\" for PostToolUse/Stop/UserPromptSubmit hooks (deprecated for PreToolUse, use hookSpecificOutput.permissionDecision instead)\n- `reason` - Explanation for decision\n- `hookSpecificOutput` - Event-specific output (must include `hookEventName`):\n  - `additionalContext` - Text injected into model context\n  - `permissionDecision` - \"allow\", \"deny\", or \"ask\" (PreToolUse only)\n  - `permissionDecisionReason` - Reason for the permission decision (PreToolUse only)\n  - `updatedInput` - Modified tool input (PreToolUse only)\n\n### Common Patterns\n\n**Auto-format after writes:**\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PostToolUse\": [{\n      \"matcher\": \"Write|Edit\",\n      \"hooks\": [{\n        \"type\": \"command\",\n        \"command\": \"jq -r '.tool_response.filePath // .tool_input.file_path' | { read -r f; prettier --write \\\"$f\\\"; } 2>/dev/null || true\"\n      }]\n    }]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Log all bash commands:**\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PreToolUse\": [{\n      \"matcher\": \"Bash\",\n      \"hooks\": [{\n        \"type\": \"command\",\n        \"command\": \"jq -r '.tool_input.command' >> ~/.claude/bash-log.txt\"\n      }]\n    }]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Stop hook that displays message to user:**\n\nCommand must output JSON with `systemMessage` field:\n```bash\n# Example command that outputs: {\"systemMessage\": \"Session complete!\"}\necho '{\"systemMessage\": \"Session complete!\"}'\n```\n\n**Run tests after code changes:**\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PostToolUse\": [{\n      \"matcher\": \"Write|Edit\",\n      \"hooks\": [{\n        \"type\": \"command\",\n        \"command\": \"jq -r '.tool_input.file_path // .tool_response.filePath' | grep -E '\\\\.(ts|js)$' && npm test || true\"\n      }]\n    }]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n\n## Constructing a Hook (with verification)\n\nGiven an event, matcher, target file, and desired behavior, follow this flow. Each step catches a different failure class — a hook that silently does nothing is worse than no hook.\n\n1. **Dedup check.** Read the target file. If a hook already exists on the same event+matcher, show the existing command and ask: keep it, replace it, or add alongside.\n\n2. **Construct the command for THIS project — don't assume.** The hook receives JSON on stdin. Build a command that:\n   - Extracts any needed payload safely — use `jq -r` into a quoted variable or `{ read -r f; ... \"$f\"; }`, NOT unquoted `| xargs` (splits on spaces)\n   - Invokes the underlying tool the way this project runs it (npx/bunx/yarn/pnpm? Makefile target? globally-installed?)\n   - Skips inputs the tool doesn't handle (formatters often have `--ignore-unknown`; if not, guard by extension)\n   - Stays RAW for now — no `|| true`, no stderr suppression. You'll wrap it after the pipe-test passes.\n\n3. **Pipe-test the raw command.** Synthesize the stdin payload the hook will receive and pipe it directly:\n   - `Pre|PostToolUse` on `Write|Edit`: `echo '{\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"<a real file from this repo>\"}}' | <cmd>`\n   - `Pre|PostToolUse` on `Bash`: `echo '{\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"ls\"}}' | <cmd>`\n   - `Stop`/`UserPromptSubmit`/`SessionStart`: most commands don't read stdin, so `echo '{}' | <cmd>` suffices\n\n   Check exit code AND side effect (file actually formatted, test actually ran). If it fails you get a real error — fix (wrong package manager? tool not installed? jq path wrong?) and retest. Once it works, wrap with `2>/dev/null || true` (unless the user wants a blocking check).\n\n4. **Write the JSON.** Merge into the target file (schema shape in the \"Hook Structure\" section above). If this creates `.claude/settings.local.json` for the first time, add it to .gitignore — the Write tool doesn't auto-gitignore it.\n\n5. **Validate syntax + schema in one shot:**\n\n   `jq -e '.hooks.<event>[] | select(.matcher == \"<matcher>\") | .hooks[] | select(.type == \"command\") | .command' <target-file>`\n\n   Exit 0 + prints your command = correct. Exit 4 = matcher doesn't match. Exit 5 = malformed JSON or wrong nesting. A broken settings.json silently disables ALL settings from that file — fix any pre-existing malformation too.\n\n6. **Prove the hook fires** — only for `Pre|PostToolUse` on a matcher you can trigger in-turn (`Write|Edit` via Edit, `Bash` via Bash). `Stop`/`UserPromptSubmit`/`SessionStart` fire outside this turn — skip to step 7.\n\n   For a **formatter** on `PostToolUse`/`Write|Edit`: introduce a detectable violation via Edit (two consecutive blank lines, bad indentation, missing semicolon — something this formatter corrects; NOT trailing whitespace, Edit strips that before writing), re-read, confirm the hook **fixed** it. For **anything else**: temporarily prefix the command in settings.json with `echo \"$(date) hook fired\" >> /tmp/claude-hook-check.txt; `, trigger the matching tool (Edit for `Write|Edit`, a harmless `true` for `Bash`), read the sentinel file.\n\n   **Always clean up** — revert the violation, strip the sentinel prefix — whether the proof passed or failed.\n\n   **If proof fails but pipe-test passed and `jq -e` passed**: the settings watcher isn't watching `.claude/` — it only watches directories that had a settings file when this session started. The hook is written correctly. Tell the user to open `/hooks` once (reloads config) or restart — you can't do this yourself; `/hooks` is a user UI menu and opening it ends this turn.\n\n7. **Handoff.** Tell the user the hook is live (or needs `/hooks`/restart per the watcher caveat). Point them at `/hooks` to review, edit, or disable it later. The UI only shows \"Ran N hooks\" if a hook errors or is slow — silent success is invisible by design.\n\n\n## Example Workflows\n\n### Adding a Hook\n\nUser: \"Format my code after Claude writes it\"\n\n1. **Clarify**: Which formatter? (prettier, gofmt, etc.)\n2. **Read**: `.claude/settings.json` (or create if missing)\n3. **Merge**: Add to existing hooks, don't replace\n4. **Result**:\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PostToolUse\": [{\n      \"matcher\": \"Write|Edit\",\n      \"hooks\": [{\n        \"type\": \"command\",\n        \"command\": \"jq -r '.tool_response.filePath // .tool_input.file_path' | { read -r f; prettier --write \\\"$f\\\"; } 2>/dev/null || true\"\n      }]\n    }]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Adding Permissions\n\nUser: \"Allow npm commands without prompting\"\n\n1. **Read**: Existing permissions\n2. **Merge**: Add `Bash(npm *)` to allow array\n3. **Result**: Combined with existing allows\n\n### Environment Variables\n\nUser: \"Set DEBUG=true\"\n\n1. **Decide**: User settings (global) or project settings?\n2. **Read**: Target file\n3. **Merge**: Add to env object\n```json\n{ \"env\": { \"DEBUG\": \"true\" } }\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes to Avoid\n\n1. **Replacing instead of merging** - Always preserve existing settings\n2. **Wrong file** - Ask user if scope is unclear\n3. **Invalid JSON** - Validate syntax after changes\n4. **Forgetting to read first** - Always read before write\n\n## Troubleshooting Hooks\n\nIf a hook isn't running:\n1. **Check the settings file** - Read ~/.claude/settings.json or .claude/settings.json\n2. **Verify JSON syntax** - Invalid JSON silently fails\n3. **Check the matcher** - Does it match the tool name? (e.g., \"Bash\", \"Write\", \"Edit\")\n4. **Check hook type** - Is it \"command\", \"prompt\", or \"agent\"?\n5. **Test the command** - Run the hook command manually to see if it works\n6. **Use --debug** - Run `claude --debug` to see hook execution logs\n\n\n## Full Settings JSON Schema\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"$schema\": {\n      \"description\": \"JSON Schema reference for Claude Code settings\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"apiKeyHelper\": {\n      \"description\": \"Path to a script that outputs authentication values\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"proxyAuthHelper\": {\n      \"description\": \"Shell command that outputs a Proxy-Authorization header value (EAP)\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"awsCredentialExport\": {\n      \"description\": \"Path to a script that exports AWS credentials\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"awsAuthRefresh\": {\n      \"description\": \"Path to a script that refreshes AWS authentication\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"gcpAuthRefresh\": {\n      \"description\": \"Command to refresh GCP authentication (e.g., gcloud auth application-default login)\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"processWrapper\": {\n      \"description\": \"Corporate launcher argv prefix for the background-agent supervisor, the sessions and workers it hosts, and the other covered background processes listed in the Claude Code corporate-launcher documentation. Equivalent to the CLAUDE_CODE_PROCESS_WRAPPER environment variable, which takes precedence when set. Honored from managed settings, a --settings/SDK-supplied settings file, and user settings, in that precedence order; project and local settings are ignored.\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"policyHelper\": {\n      \"description\": \"Executable that computes managed settings at startup. Honored only from admin-controlled policy sources.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"path\": {\n          \"description\": \"Absolute path to the helper executable\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"timeoutMs\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1000,\n          \"maximum\": 9007199254740991\n        },\n        \"refreshIntervalMs\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"number\",\n              \"const\": 0\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"integer\",\n              \"minimum\": 60000,\n              \"maximum\": 9007199254740991\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"path\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"fileSuggestion\": {\n      \"description\": \"Custom file suggestion configuration for @ mentions\",\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"type\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"const\": \"command\"\n        },\n        \"command\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"command\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"respectGitignore\": {\n      \"description\": \"Whether file picker should respect .gitignore files (default: true). Note: .ignore files are always respected.\",\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"cleanupPeriodDays\": {\n      \"description\": \"Number of days to retain chat transcripts before automatic cleanup (default: 30). Minimum 1. Use a large value for long retention; use --no-session-persistence to disable transcript writes entirely.\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\",\n      \"exclusiveMinimum\": 0,\n      \"maximum\": 9007199254740991\n    },\n    \"desktopSessionCleanupPeriodDays\": {\n      \"description\": \"Retention ceiling in days for session transcripts created or last written by a desktop-host surface (Claude Desktop, Cowork), which are otherwise exempt from the cleanupPeriodDays sweep. 0 (the default) means no ceiling: such transcripts are kept until deleted another way. Unlike cleanupPeriodDays, 0 is allowed because this setting never disables writes — it only bounds an exemption from deletion. The ceiling is a hard cap: it also bounds an active archive grace, so the grace window of a release marker never keeps files past the ceiling. Ignored when cleanupPeriodDays is managed by org policy. A ceiling at or below cleanupPeriodDays effectively disables the exemption: those transcripts age out on the regular cleanupPeriodDays schedule, so the effective retention is whichever of the two periods is longer.\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\",\n      \"minimum\": 0,\n      \"maximum\": 9007199254740991\n    },\n    \"syncClaudeAiSkills\": {\n      \"description\": \"Set to false to turn off syncing of the skills you have enabled on claude.ai. In your user settings (or managed settings): nothing more is downloaded, previously synced skills (~/.cla\n\n[... skill content truncated for compaction; use Read on the skill path if you need the full text]\n\n---\n\n### Skill: sc4sap:config-to-document\nPath: plugin:sc4sap:config-to-document\n\nBase directory for this skill: C:\\Users\\pssps\\.claude\\plugins\\cache\\sc4sap\\sc4sap\\0.6.35\\skills\\config-to-document\n\n# SC4SAP Configuration → Document\r\n\r\nReads the module's IMG structure and configuration tables from the live system and writes **one HTML file**: an IMG tree with search and status filters on the left, one page per IMG activity (screen drawing with the real values, the full value table, customer changes, checks, SAP documentation) and a checklist panel on the right.\r\n\r\n<Purpose>\r\nConsultants, key users and auditors need to know how a system is set up — not how SAP describes the module in general. This skill answers \"what is configured here, what did the project change, and what looks wrong\" from the system itself. GUI screenshots are not possible, so the screens are drawn with the shared screen renderer (the same drawing as `program-to-manual`), filled with the values read from the tables.\r\n</Purpose>\r\n\r\n<Response_Prefix>Every response triggered by this skill MUST begin with `[Model: <main-model> · Dispatched: <sub-summary>]` per [`../../common/model-routing-rule.md`](../../common/model-routing-rule.md) § Response Prefix Convention.</Response_Prefix>\r\n\r\n<Team_Mode>**No teamMode integration.** Extraction and drawing are scripted; agents only write and review the consultant notes (Step 4).</Team_Mode>\r\n\r\n<Use_When>\r\n- \"설정 문서\", \"컨피그 리스트\", \"configuration list\", \"IMG 설정 정리\", \"SPRO 설정 문서화\", \"설정 점검\", \"config audit\", \"how is MM configured in this system\"\r\n- Go-live / handover / audit: the configuration must be written down as it is\r\n- Before a rollout or a system copy: what did the project change in the IMG\r\n</Use_When>\r\n\r\n<Do_Not_Use_When>\r\n- One program's behaviour → `/sc4sap:program-to-spec` or `/sc4sap:program-to-manual`\r\n- A question about one setting → `/sc4sap:ask-consultant` (answers in chat)\r\n- Business-process documentation of a custom package → `/sc4sap:package-to-process`\r\n</Do_Not_Use_When>\r\n\r\n<Decisions_Fixed>\r\nSettled when the skill was designed — do not ask again:\r\n- **Real values, as they are.** The document shows the table values exactly as read (organisation names included). It is an internal document; say so once in the closing message.\r\n- **Read-only.** Only customizing / system tables (delivery class C, G, E, S), DDIC metadata and the transport key tables are read — on ECC through `ZMCP_ADT_DISPATCH` `TABLE_READ`, which refuses everything else. The MCP blocklist still applies; a refused table shows as \"Not readable\" in the document, never as a failure.\r\n- **Customer change = customer transport.** A row counts as customer-changed when a non-SAP transport (`E071K`, `TRKORR NOT LIKE 'SAP%'`) recorded its key, in any client.\r\n- **Language.** Texts (IMG titles, field labels, value texts) in the document language when the system has them, else English. SAP documentation is mostly English.\r\n- **One file.** HTML with data and drawings embedded; works offline; prints.\r\n</Decisions_Fixed>\r\n\r\n<Inputs>\r\n- Module (required): `MM` today. `SD`, `PP`, `PM`, `QM`, `LE`, `PS`, `CO` resolve through the same IMG walk (`--module X`); only MM has check rules (`configs/MM/config-checks.json`) yet — other modules get the built-in checks.\r\n- Areas (optional): IMG areas under the module node — default all.\r\n- Language (optional): from `.sc4sap/config.json` (`language`), else `ko`.\r\n</Inputs>\r\n\r\n<Workflow>\r\n\r\n**Step 1 — Module and preflight.** Take the module from the arguments; if missing, ask with `AskUserQuestion` (MM first, recommended). Confirm the active profile (`.sc4sap/active-profile.txt`) in one line.\r\n\r\n**Step 2 — Areas.** Run\r\n```\r\nnode scripts/config/extract-config.mjs --module <M> --list-areas\r\n```\r\nShow the areas (document language + English) and ask with one `AskUserQuestion` (`multiSelect: true`, first option \"All areas (Recommended)\"). A full MM run reads about 1,300 tables (15–25 minutes on ECC); say so when the user picks all.\r\n\r\nIf the command fails with `TABLE_READ: table … is not allowed` on an IMG table (`TNODEIMG`, `CUS_IMGACH`), the system's `ZMCP_ADT_DISPATCH` predates the customizing allow rule: stop and tell the user to update it from `abap/zmcp_adt_dispatch_ecc.abap` (setup Step 9) — never work around the dispatcher.\r\n\r\n**Step 3 — Extract.** Run in the background (`run_in_background: true`):\r\n```\r\nnode scripts/config/extract-config.mjs --module <M> [--areas \"<Area 1>,<Area 2>\"] [--lang <lang>]\r\n```\r\nIt prints progress (`tables n/N`) on stderr and one JSON line at the end: `{ ok, file, counts }`. An interrupted run resumes from its read cache; `--fresh` starts over (use it when the user asks for a refresh of an earlier document). Report the counts when it finishes.\r\n\r\n**Step 4 — Consultant notes and reference material (written, then reviewed).** Per IMG activity the notes card (purpose, effect of *this system's* values, cautions, references) and the reference panel (SAP documentation summarised in the document language, 2–3 setup cases with flow diagrams and which one this system follows, comparison table, decision checklist, decision criteria, official SAP sources — Help Portal, Notes / KBAs, Learning — opened and cited) are written by the module consultant agent and reviewed by `sap-critic`; never by the main thread. Prompts: [`notes-prompts.md`](notes-prompts.md) — use them verbatim with the placeholders filled.\r\n0. **Terms first.** `node scripts/config/notes.mjs terms --module <M>` → `terms/_in/tNNN.json` (names SAP has no document-language text for: IMG folders, activity titles, field labels; 150 per batch; translated terms are reused by later runs). Per batch: writer then reviewer, prompt § 4. Skip when it reports 0 terms.\r\n1. **Scope — ask on every run.** `node scripts/config/notes.mjs scopes --module <M>` prints activities and batches per scope (activities with reviewed notes from earlier runs are left out). Ask with one `AskUserQuestion`, each option labelled with its numbers from that output and the cost (one batch ≈ 12 activities, a writer, a reviewer and usually a revision run with web research — measured on MM: about 750k tokens and 40 minutes per batch):\r\n   - `custom` — activities customer transports changed (Recommended)\r\n   - `values` — also standard and empty ones (every activity with a table)\r\n   - `all` — every activity, including transaction-only ones\r\n   - `none` — no notes this run; the document is built without new notes\r\n   Then `node scripts/config/notes.mjs batches --module <M> --scope <scope> --size 12` → `notes/_in/bNNN.json` (numbered after existing batches; `--redo` rewrites reviewed activities too, only when the user asks).\r\n2. **Write** — per batch, `Agent(subagent_type: \"sc4sap:sap-<m>-consultant\")` with prompt § 1 (saves `--kind draft`). Batches run in parallel, at most 4 at a time.\r\n3. **Review** — per batch, prompt § 2: (a) `notes-lint.mjs` on the main thread (sources, transactions, counts, check findings — no tokens), (b) `sc4sap:sap-critic` judges SAP meaning with the lint facts in hand and opens only sources the lint marks `new` / `changed` (saves `--kind review`, prints the `fix` list). Saving a review adds the sources of every `ok` activity to the verified-source cache, which later batches receive as `knownSources`; `notes.mjs sources --module <M>` seeds that cache from batches reviewed before it existed.\r\n4. **Revise** — for a batch with `fix` items, the writer agent again with prompt § 3 (saves `--kind revised`). One round; findings still open after it stay visible in the document (\"Review findings open\").\r\n5. `node scripts/config/notes.mjs status --module <M>` must show draft + review for every batch of this run before Step 5 (skip this step with scope `none`).\r\n6. **Knowledge base.** `node scripts/config/notes.mjs kb --module <M>` copies the general part of every reviewed note (purpose, SAP documentation summary, cases without the verdicts, comparison, checklist, criteria, official sources) to `~/.sc4sap/kb/config/<M>/<lang>/`. Later runs — this system again or any other system — mark those activities `\"mode\": \"system\"` in their batches: the writer adds only impact, cautions and one verdict per case, with no web research, and the reviewer checks only that part. On MM this cuts a batch to a fraction of the first-run cost.\r\n\r\n**Step 5 — Build.**\r\n```\r\nnode scripts/config/build-config-doc.mjs --module <M> [--lang <lang>] [--import <edited.html>]\r\n```\r\nOutput: `<artifactBase>/config-docs/<M>/<M>-config-v<n>-<lang>.html` (`status` counts, checks with findings and `edited` notes in the JSON line). When the user hands back a page saved from edit mode, build with `--import <file>`: its edits merge into `notes/edits.json` (per activity or view the newer edit wins; a page from another system or module is refused) and every later build keeps them — edited views replace their values, card title and history and are drawn again. Edits never enter the knowledge base.\r\n\r\n**Step 6 — Close.** Report in the user's language:\r\n- the file path, IMG activities by status (customized / standard / not set / no values / not readable),\r\n- the check findings by severity, error ones by title,\r\n- tables that could not be read, and why (blocklist, dispatcher),\r\n- one line: the document holds the system's real configuration values — share it internally only.\r\n\r\nDo not paste table contents into chat.\r\n</Workflow>\r\n\r\n<Document_Contents>\r\nPer IMG activity: IMG path, title (document language + English), status badge, T-codes, consultant notes with their review state, objects (view / view cluster / table), row and customer-row counts; for each view an SM30 overview drawn with the first rows (customer rows first) and, for wide views, a detail screen of one row; the full value table (key columns bold, fixed-value texts next to codes, customer rows highlighted with their transports, filter and \"customer rows only\"); the customer transports that touched the table (date, request, user, description); checks for the activity; SAP's IMG documentation. Overview: counts by status, areas with status bars, recent customer transports. Right panel: all check findings, click to jump.\r\n\r\nEdit mode (\"Edit\" in the top bar, nothing installed): the consultant notes and the reference panel become editable plain text — add or delete list items, add notes to an activity without them, delete a source — and so do the views: card title, value-table cells (rows added or deleted) and the change-history rows. Edited notes and views carry an \"Edited · author · date\" badge, so readers see where the page differs from the system; an edited view's SM30 drawing is drawn again from the edited rows at the next `--import` build. Any drawing (overview or detail) can be replaced by a real screenshot — \"Use screenshot\", or click the drawing and Ctrl+V; \"Original screen\" brings the drawing back; captures wider than 1800 px are scaled down. Undo (Ctrl+Z / button), autosave to the browser with \"continue editing\" on reopen. \"Save\" asks for author and change note and downloads the page with every edit embedded (`<script id=\"config-edits\">`) — the file to hand back for `--import`.\r\n</Document_Contents>\r\n\r\n<Checks>\r\nBuilt-in: activities whose values could not be read. Module rules: `configs/<M>/config-checks.json` — `reads` (extra tables the rules need) and `rules` of type `exists` (every row of A has its counterpart in B), `assigned` (every row of A is used by B) and `custom-keys` (customer name-space entries). Add a rule there instead of hard-coding checks; each rule names its tables, so it attaches itself to the IMG activities that maintain them.\r\n</Checks>\r\n\r\n<Files>\r\n- `scripts/config/extract-config.mjs` — IMG walk, values, transports, docs → `config-docs/<M>/snapshot.json`\r\n- `scripts/config/sap-reader.mjs` — MCP client, SELECT * reads, IN-list chunking, read cache\r\n- `scripts/config/itf.mjs` — SAP documentation (ITF) → blocks\r\n- `scripts/config/notes.mjs` — note and term batches, marker-text parsing, merge of drafts / reviews / revisions, knowledge base (`kb`), source-cache seeding (`sources`)\r\n- `scripts/config/notes-sources.mjs` — verified-source cache `~/.sc4sap/kb/config/<M>/sources-<lang>.json` (status, record, hints)\r\n- `scripts/config/notes-lint.mjs` — mechanical batch checks before review; t-code cache `~/.sc4sap/kb/tcodes/<system>.json`\r\n- `scripts/config/config-checks.mjs` — rule engine\r\n- `scripts/config/build-config-doc.mjs` + `config-doc-page.mjs` — model, screen drawings, page, `--import` of edits\r\n- `scripts/config/config-doc-editor.mjs` — edit mode (styles, client script, labels)\r\n</Files>\r\n\n\nARGUMENTS: SD 모듈을 해줘.\n\nThe following tools just became available and are ready to use:\nReadNotifications\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__batch\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__guide\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__update\n\nThe following deferred tools are now available via ToolSearch. Their schemas are NOT loaded — calling them directly will fail with InputValidationError. Use ToolSearch with query \"select:<name>[,<name>...]\" to load tool schemas before calling them:\nArtifactComments\nArtifactData\nCronCreate\nCronDelete\nCronList\nDesignSync\nEndConversation\nEnterPlanMode\nEnterWorktree\nExitPlanMode\nExitWorktree\nFetchInboxMessage\nMonitor\nNotebookEdit\nPushNotification\nRemoteTrigger\nSendMessage\nSendUserFile\nTaskStop\nWebFetch\nWebSearch\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__browser_batch\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__computer\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__file_upload\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__find\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__form_input\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__get_page_text\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__gif_creator\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__javascript_tool\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__list_connected_browsers\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__navigate\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__read_console_messages\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__read_network_requests\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__read_page\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__resize_window\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__select_browser\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__shortcuts_execute\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__shortcuts_list\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__switch_browser\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_close_mcp\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp\nmcp__claude-in-chrome__upload_image\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__create\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__delete\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__export\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__query\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__read\nmcp__claude_ai_Google_Drive__authenticate\nmcp__claude_ai_Google_Drive__complete_authentication\nmcp__claude_ai_Notion__authenticate\nmcp__claude_ai_Notion__complete_authentication\nmcp__composio__authenticate\nmcp__composio__complete_authentication\nmcp__ide__executeCode\nmcp__ide__getDiagnostics\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ActivateObjects\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateBehaviorDefinition\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateBehaviorImplementation\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateCdsUnitTest\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateClass\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateDataElement\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateDomain\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateFunctionGroup\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateFunctionModule\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateGuiStatus\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateInclude\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateInterface\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateMetadataExtension\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreatePackage\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateProgram\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateScreen\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateServiceBinding\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateServiceDefinition\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateStructure\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateTable\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateTextElement\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateTransport\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateUnitTest\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__CreateView\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteBehaviorDefinition\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteBehaviorImplementation\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteCdsUnitTest\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteClass\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteDataElement\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteDomain\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteFunctionGroup\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteFunctionModule\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteGuiStatus\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteInclude\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteInterface\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteLocalDefinitions\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteLocalMacros\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteLocalTestClass\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteLocalTypes\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteMetadataExtension\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteProgram\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteScreen\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteServiceBinding\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteServiceDefinition\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteStructure\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteTable\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteTextElement\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteUnitTest\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DeleteView\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__DescribeByList\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetAbapAST\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetAbapSemanticAnalysis\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetAbapSystemSymbols\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetAdtTypes\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetBadiImplementations\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetBehaviorDefinition\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetBehaviorImplementation\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetCdsUnitTest\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetCdsUnitTestResult\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetCdsUnitTestStatus\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetClass\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetDataElement\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetDomain\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetEnhancementImpl\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetEnhancementSpot\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetEnhancements\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetFunctionGroup\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetFunctionModule\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetGuiStatus\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetGuiStatusList\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetInactiveObjects\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetInclude\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetIncludesList\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetInterface\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetJobUsage\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetLocalDefinitions\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetLocalMacros\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetLocalTestClass\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetLocalTypes\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetMetadataExtension\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetNodeStructureLow\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetObjectInfo\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetObjectNodeFromCache\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetObjectStructure\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetObjectStructureLow\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetObjectsByType\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetObjectsList\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetPackage\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetPackageContents\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetPackageTree\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetProgFullCode\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetProgram\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetScreen\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetScreensList\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetServiceBinding\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetServiceDefinition\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetSession\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetSqlQuery\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetStructure\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetTable\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetTableContents\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetTcodeUsage\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetTextElement\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetTransaction\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetTransport\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetTypeInfo\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetUnitTest\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetUnitTestResult\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetUnitTestStatus\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetUsageSnippets\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetView\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetVirtualFoldersLow\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__GetWhereUsed\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ListServiceBindingTypes\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ListTransports\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__PatchGuiStatus\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadBehaviorDefinition\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadBehaviorImplementation\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadClass\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadDataElement\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadDomain\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadFunctionGroup\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadFunctionModule\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadGuiStatus\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadInterface\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadMetadataExtension\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadPackage\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadProgram\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadScreen\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadServiceBinding\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadServiceDefinition\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadStructure\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadTable\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadTextElementsBulk\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReadView\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ReloadProfile\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RunUnitTest\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeAnalyzeDump\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeAnalyzeProfilerTrace\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeCreateProfilerTraceParameters\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeGetDumpById\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeGetGatewayErrorLog\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeGetProfilerTraceData\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeListDumps\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeListFeeds\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeListProfilerTraceFiles\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeListSystemMessages\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeRunClassWithProfiling\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__RuntimeRunProgramWithProfiling\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__SearchObject\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateBehaviorDefinition\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateBehaviorImplementation\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateCdsUnitTest\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateClass\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateDataElement\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateDomain\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateFunctionGroup\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateFunctionModule\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateGuiStatus\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateInclude\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateInterface\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateLocalDefinitions\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateLocalMacros\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateLocalTestClass\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateLocalTypes\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateMetadataExtension\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateProgram\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateScreen\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateServiceBinding\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateServiceDefinition\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateStructure\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateTable\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateTextElement\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateUnitTest\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__UpdateView\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__ValidateServiceBinding\nmcp__plugin_sc4sap_sap__WriteTextElementsBulk\n\nAvailable agent types for the Agent tool:\n- claude: Catch-all for any task that doesn't fit a more specific agent. FleetView's default when no agent name is typed. (Tools: *)\n- claude-code-guide: Use this agent when the user asks questions (\"Can Claude...\", \"Does Claude...\", \"How do I...\") about: (1) Claude Code (the CLI tool) - features, hooks, slash commands, MCP servers, settings, IDE integrations, keyboard shortcuts; (2) Claude Agent SDK - building custom agents; (3) Claude API (formerly Anthropic API) - Messages API for directly passing messages to Claude, Tool Runner (`client.beta.messages.tool_runner`) for running an agentic loop over your own tools, manual tool-use loops, Managed Agents for server-hosted agents with a managed sandbox, prompt caching, and general Anthropic SDK usage; (4) Claude Tag (Claude in Slack) - what it is, setting it up for a Slack workspace, `/install-slack-app`; (5) `claude plugin eval` (writing and running plugin eval suites, its JSON/report, sandbox, CI) and the `/skill-doctor` report. **IMPORTANT:** Before spawning a new agent, check if there is already a running or recently completed claude-code-guide agent that you can continue via SendMessage. (Tools: Glob, Grep, Read, WebFetch, WebSearch)\n- Explore: Read-only search agent for broad fan-out searches — when answering means sweeping many files, directories, or naming conventions and you only need the conclusion, not the file dumps. It reads excerpts rather than whole files, so it locates code; it doesn't review or audit it. Specify search breadth: \"medium\" for moderate exploration, \"very thorough\" for multiple locations and naming conventions. (Tools: All tools except Agent, Artifact, ArtifactComments, ArtifactData, ArtifactCheck, ExitPlanMode, Edit, Write, NotebookEdit)\n- general-purpose: General-purpose agent for researching complex questions, searching for code, and executing multi-step tasks. When you are searching for a keyword or file and are not confident that you will find the right match in the first few tries use this agent to perform the search for you. (Tools: *)\n- Plan: Software architect agent for designing implementation plans. Use this when you need to plan the implementation strategy for a task. Returns step-by-step plans, identifies critical files, and considers architectural trade-offs. (Tools: All tools except Agent, Artifact, ArtifactComments, ArtifactData, ArtifactCheck, ExitPlanMode, Edit, Write, NotebookEdit)\n- sc4sap:sap-analyst: SAP requirements analysis — functional specifications, gap analysis, and acceptance criteria (Opus, R/O) (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, WebFetch, Web