\",\n39:    \"lint\": \"eslint src\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\pssps\\Documents\\Projects\\sc4sap_project\\sc4sap\\CHANGELOG.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":10,"newStart":11,"newLines":10,"lines":[" - The extractor reads the F1 documentation of every column's data element (`fieldDocs`); `--field-docs` adds it to an existing snapshot without reading the configuration again.\r"," - New `scripts/config/fields.mjs`: batches of 100 data elements (label, domain values, F1 text, where used, samples), written by the module consultant and corrected by `sap-critic` (prompt § 5, no web research), then kept in `~/.sc4sap/kb/fields/<lang>.json` — shared by every module, so a later module writes only the data elements it does not share.\r"," - `--full-tables \"<T1>,<T2>\"` reads the named tables up to the read cap instead of `--max-rows`; a capped table is split by its next key fields, and `config-checks.json` `reads` without a condition are read like activity tables (DDIC fields, customer transports).\r","-\r"," - BAdI customer implementations: an IMG activity that is a BAdI (`CUS_ACTEXT`) shows a card with the customer implementations of this system — classic (`SXC_EXIT` / `SXC_ATTR` / `SXC_CLASS`) and enhancement-based (`BADIIMPL_ENH`) — and an active implementation marks the activity customized; the overview lists every BAdI with customer implementations. `--badi` adds them to an existing snapshot.\r"," - Case flows and screen drawings open in a lightbox with zoom (−, +, fit, close).\r"," - SD: `configs/SD/config-checks.json` reads the SD condition tables the checks need; corrected SD pricing transactions (V/06, V/07, V/08, OVKK).\r","+\r"," ### Fixed — `config-to-document`\r"," \r"," - View selection conditions on the same field are OR-ed and NUMC values compared as numbers, so views such as output-function or billing-plan variants no longer show 0 rows."]}]}],"moreFiles"